   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to requiring the division of\nhousing and community renewal to establish a publicly accessible online\ndatabase of building-wide major capital improvements",
    "basePrintNo": "S2363",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2363-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §260-a, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2363\n\nSPONSOR: RIVERA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to requiring the division\nof housing and community renewal to establish a publicly accessible\nonline database of building-wide major capital improvements\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill requires the Division of Housing and Community Renewal (DHCR)\nto publish a database of major capital improvements (MCIs) on its\nwebsite.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the Executive Law by adding a new section 260-a to the\ndivision of housing, to require the DHCR to publish an online database\nfor all MCI applications in cities with a population of one million or\nmore that includes the cost, make and model, where the item was\npurchased, name of company or individual installing the item, and cost\nof installation.\n\nSection 2 provides an effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMajor capital improvements (MCIs) permanently raise rents for rent-regu-\nlated tenants and are often fraudulently filed or used as a displacement\ntool by landlords. Storing basic MCI information, most of which is\nalready collected by the Division of Housing and Community Renewal\n(DHCR), into an accessible online database will allow tenants to be\nempowered to fact-check MCI information filed by their landlords. This\nbill will offer tenants an effective deterrent against fraud and give\nthem the information necessary to verify the accuracy of their rent\nincreases.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-2020: S5691 Rivera/A1298 Rosenthal L\n\n2021-2022: S3325 Rivera/A2108 Rosenthal L\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSince the Division of Housing and Community Renewal already maintains a\nwebsite, the additional cost posed by this feature should be minimal.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
