    "lawCode": "Add §19-b, Pub Hous L",
    "lawSection": "Public Housing Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2363A\n\nSPONSOR: RIVERA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public housing law, in relation to requiring the\ndivision of housing and community renewal to establish a publicly acces-\nsible online database of building-wide major capital improvements\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill requires the Division of Housing and Community Renewal (DHCR)\nto publish a database of major capital improvements (MCIs) on its\nwebsite.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the Public Housing Law, as it relates to the Division\nof Housing, by adding a new section 19-b, to require the DHCR to publish\nan online database for all MCI applications in cities with a population\nof one million or more that includes the cost, make, and model, where\nthe item was purchased, name of company or individual installing the\nitem, and cost of installation.\n\nSection 2 provides an effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMajor capital improvements (MCIs) permanently raise rents for rent-regu-\nlated tenants and are often fraudulently filed or used as a displacement\ntool by landlords. Storing basic MCI information, most of which is\nalready collected by the Division of Housing and Community Renewal\n(DHCR), into an accessible online database will allow tenants to be\nempowered to fact-check MCI information filed by their landlords. This\nbill will offer tenants an effective deterrent against fraud and give\nthem the information necessary to verify the accuracy of their rent\nincreases.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-2020: S5691 Rivera/A1298 Rosenthal L\n2021-2022: S3325 Rivera/A2108 Rosenthal L\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSince the Division of Housing and Community Renewal already maintains a\nwebsite, the additional cost posed by this feature should be minimal.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill shall take effect immediately.\n",
